%description:

Tcp.delayedAckTimeout:zero -- with a timeout of 0, the delayed ACK of a lone segment goes at once.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "with delayedAcksEnabled, the longest delay of an ACK". A longest delay
of 0 is no delay.

The classes: value (a time above 0), zero (0s). This test separates "zero" from "value": with
a time above 0, the ACK waits.

Host under test: host2, the receiver, with the delayed ACK. Peer: host1 sends one segment of
100 bytes. Observation: level 1, the ACK of host2 within 1 ms of the arrival.

%# parameter: Tcp.delayedAckTimeout
%# class: zero
%# value: 0s
%# key: *.host2.tcp.delayedAckTimeout
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpDelayedAckTimeoutZero")
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
                  .describe("the segment of 100 bytes at host2")
                  .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.ackBit == true")
                  .describe("the ACK of host2, at once")
                  .within(0.001));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpDelayedAckTimeoutZero compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.delayedAckTimeout = 0s    # the parameter under test
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 100B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpDelayedAckTimeoutZero: PASS
